# DESCRIPTION

This is a serializer engine that allows you to turn Perl data structures into
[Data::Dumper](https://metacpan.org/pod/Data%3A%3ADumper) output and vice-versa.

Since version 2.2.0 of [Dancer2](https://metacpan.org/pod/Dancer2), the Dumper serializer is no longer
shipped as part of the core framework, but is available as its own CPAN
distribution, `Dancer2-Serializer-Dumper`. Install this distribution if you
want to use it, and add its dependencies to your application.

# SECURITY

The `deserialize` method evaluates the content as Perl code, inside a
[Safe](https://metacpan.org/pod/Safe) compartment. [Safe](https://metacpan.org/pod/Safe) is not a real security sandbox, so this
serializer must never be used to deserialize untrusted input. [Dancer2](https://metacpan.org/pod/Dancer2)'s
[Dancer2::Serializer::Mutable](https://metacpan.org/pod/Dancer2%3A%3ASerializer%3A%3AMutable) serializer therefore leaves the Dumper
serializer disabled by default: if you really want to opt in to it, you must
set `enable_dumper` in your Mutable serializer configuration, and you must
have this distribution installed.

# METHODS

Returns 'text/x-data-dumper'

